WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
The UK, 2025.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:08.450
Trussell food banks gave out over
2.6 million emergency parcels.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.590
Somalia, 2026.

4
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.690
The Global Hunger Index ranked
it 122nd of 122 countries.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.930
One is a high-income country.

6
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.930
The other is low-income.

7
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.230
So what does going without enough
food mean for a family in each place?

8
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.850
Is it the same thing, just
more of it in Somalia?

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.610
Or only a matter of prices?

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.910
In this mission, you'll pin
down what food security means,

11
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.650
and break it into four parts.

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.690
Then you'll compare the
two places, row by row,

13
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.070
from scale to safety nets.

14
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.650
Your mission: compare what going without
enough food means for families in the

15
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.350
UK and Somalia.
